      "writtenOn": "2023-10-06T00:41:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we can use `EX_UNSUPPORTED_OPERATION` and `EX_SERVICE_SPECIFIC` from https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/native/libs/binder/ndk/include_ndk/android/binder_status.h;drc\u003dce8d982b30ffbf490b151c0acab4e05a61b53ba7;l\u003d103 instead of `UNIMPLEMENTED` and `INTERNAL_ERROR` respectively.\n\nHowever, the Android binder error code space and our error code space overlap. Is there any recommendation of any error code space that we should not overlap with when defining AIDL errors?\n\nThere are other existing AIDLs (e.g. Keymint) which define these types of error codes (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:hardware/interfaces/security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/ErrorCode.aidl;l\u003d112).\n\nIf you have a strong preference on using the binder error codes, I can certainly change this. In that case, can you please let me know which rust crate that I can find the definition of these error codes (to be used from our implementation)?\n\nThank you!",
