      "writtenOn": "2023-10-19T01:09:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Steven for the pointer!\n\nWhen trying to incorporate this change, I realized that there is a problem.\n\nThis AIDL is to be implemented by a Trusted applet (e.g. SecretKeeper, Keymint, Gatekeeper, etc) implemented by the vendors, running in the secure hardware.\n(This is not an AIDL for a system component)\nWe provide the reference implementation in Rust (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/authgraph/core/)\nIn the implementation of the Trusted applet code, we cannot assume the availability of the binder dependencies. Therefore, I think we cannot use the binder errors in this case.\n\nHowever, we do use the binder errors in the hal service implementation, which lives in the Android side and therefore has access to the binder dependencies: e.g. https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/system/authgraph/+/2786459/2/hal/src/lib.rs#136 \n\nPlease let me know if the above understanding is not correct.\n\nThank you!",
