      "writtenOn": "2023-10-05T20:16:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: if it\u0027s only used for one method, define it in place?\n\ninterface Foo {\n    parcelable Result { ... }\n    Result foo();\n}\n\nThis is in a parcelable to make extending it easier? I see a lot of single parcelables that contain a single byte array. I get it makes things more typed, but it\u0027s also a lot of layers of indirection.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 22,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "db55d492284904a64b74499c49f89d4e96de859c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9bd376d0_1f2f00b0",
        "filename": "security/authgraph/aidl/android/hardware/security/authgraph/KEAuthCompleteResult.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 35
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1678423
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-06T00:41:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The two main reasons behind the single parcelables that contain a single byte array are:\n1. They have a CDDL.\n2. They are re-used across multiple return types and method inputs.\n\nE.g. \ni. `Arc` (has `Arc.cddl` and is part of `Key` type, `SessionInfo` type, `sharedKeys` input and output of `authenticationComplete` method)\nii. `Identity` (has `Identity.cddl` and is part of `SessionInitiationInfo`, input for `init` and `finish` methods)\niii. `SessionIdSignature` (has `SessionIdSignature.cddl` and is part of `SessionInfo` type and input for `finish` and `authenticationComplete`)\niv. `PlainPubKey` (has `PlainPubKey.cddl` and is one variant of `PubKey`. `PubKey` is part of the `Key` type and inputs for `init` and `finish` methods. `Key` is in turn part of `SessioInitiationInfo` type)\nv. `SignedPubKey` (has `SignedPubKey.cddl` and is one variant of `PubKey`. `PubKey` is part of the `Key` type.\n\nSo the main motivation for having them as parcelables are: isolation of the definition and re-usability in multiple places. \n\nWe haven\u0027t defined parcels for other primitive types which do not have a specific definition - such as `peerNonce` (of type `byte[]`) and `version` (of type `int`) used as inputs for `init` and `finish`.\n\nHowever, in the above analysis I realized that we can get rid of the KEAuthCompleteResult parcelable, because it is not re-used anywhere. So I removed it and marked the return type to be an array of Arcs (the array only contains two elements)\n\nPlease let me know if you have further questions/feedback on this. Thanks!",
      "parentUuid": "a89d8e27_74059f03",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 22,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 0
      },
